# The other shape of the SAME C symbol, in its own module, through a door of
# its own.
#
# `printf` again, at a string. Until 2026-11-10 this module bound it
# directly, `printf(format: cstr lent, value: cstr)`, the value a lease
# handed past the `...` (panel 217's R3(c)); since panel 243's R1 (defect
# 2421) nothing is bound there, so `as_text.h` defines `say_text`, taking a
# `const char *` that the string is lent to for the call, `lent` because
# `printf` reads it while it runs and keeps nothing.

extern "as_text.h"
    function say_text(s: cstr lent) -> i32

# The wrapper takes a `str` and lends it inside itself, the shape §4.19
# prescribes: a wrapper taking `cstr` is a Heroes parameter no mark can reach.
function say(value: str) -> i32
    return say_text(s: value.cstr())
